From: Linus Walleij <linusw@kernel.org>
Subject: [PATCH] serial: bcm63xx: keep the console enabled on tty shutdown

Closing or hanging up a tty calls bcm_uart_shutdown() even when the
port also serves as the kernel console. Disabling the baud generator
and transmitter there prevents subsequent console writes from reaching
the wire, and flushing the TX FIFO can discard console output.

On the XG6846B, the serial capture ends at procd's SIGTERM message and
resumes at the boot loader. Terminal hangup when the console shell exits
provides a possible explanation for the missing final reboot messages.

Keep the console UART enabled and preserve its FIFO contents. Still mask
interrupts and release the IRQ for both console and ordinary tty ports.
Perform the register updates under the port lock to serialize against
console writes.

Assisted-by: Codex:GPT-6
Signed-off-by: Linus Walleij <linusw@kernel.org>
---
--- a/drivers/tty/serial/bcm63xx_uart.c
+++ b/drivers/tty/serial/bcm63xx_uart.c
@@ -455,10 +455,13 @@ static void bcm_uart_shutdown(struct uart_port *port)
 
 	uart_port_lock_irqsave(port, &flags);
 	bcm_uart_writel(port, 0, UART_IR_REG);
+	/* TTY hangup must not disable the kernel console. */
+	if (!uart_console(port)) {
+		bcm_uart_disable(port);
+		bcm_uart_flush(port);
+	}
 	uart_port_unlock_irqrestore(port, flags);
 
-	bcm_uart_disable(port);
-	bcm_uart_flush(port);
 	free_irq(port->irq, port);
 }
 
